# Regression: loading an SGF while a slow engine is thinking used to hang the
# whole application. GTP cannot abort a command in flight, and the UI thread
# waited for the game loop to stop — which it could not until the engine replied.
#
# Loading discards the current game, so the pending move is worthless: the work
# is now deferred to the game thread, which drops the move and then loads.
# See docs/adr/0001-engine-exclusive-actions.md.
#
# Uses the slow-mock bot (--delay-ms) so an engine really is mid-genmove when
# the load is requested. Without the fix this scenario times out.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black slowmock
switch_player white slowmock
wait_idle

start
# Wait only for the match to be under way; do NOT wait for idle, the whole
# point is to act while an engine is thinking.
wait_until move_count >= 1
expect running true

# Request the load mid-genmove. This must return immediately.
load_sgf tests/data/simple.sgf

# The load lands once the engine's move arrives and is discarded. Wait on the
# board size: main_line_moves is ambiguous here, because the bots' own moves
# would satisfy it just as well.
wait_until board_size 19
wait_idle
expect board_size 19
expect main_line_moves >= 4
expect navigating true

# And the app is still alive and responsive afterwards.
navigate_start
wait_idle
expect view_position 0
expect black_stones 0
expect white_stones 0
